{"actor": "unknown-agent", "data": {"documentation_gaps": {"HYPOTHESES.md": ["experiment_result"]}, "duration_s": 3445.8, "landed_paths": 0, "missing_artifacts": 0, "next": "E171: E168's unrun G3 -- does an attempt grounded in the component's published version history recover rows the unaided attempt fails, declared bar >= 0.60 -- is now the only experiment left on this record where the candidate mechanism is not the incumbent, and E170 has removed its search arm. It needs a fresh blinded version_pinned sample; this host has 7 of 300 Stack Exchange requests remaining today, so the draw waits for the daily reset. E172 (fresh observation in an untouched domain, by a stated rule) needs no quota and can run in parallel. E170's own replication gate is deliberately not run: a replication of a near-zero effect teaches nothing this record lacks.", "outcome": "worked", "push_requested": false, "summary": "E170 measured the one question E168 and E169 both left open -- is a published fix reachable by the query a developer types -- on two live ranked indexes with queries committed before any fetch. Capability controls pass on both surfaces (in:title returns the target at rank 1 on 11/13 via api.github.com/search/issues and 10/13 via github.com/search?type=issues), so the arms are readable. On the web surface the developer's quoted error string reaches the fix on 1 of the 8 rows that have a literal and component+symptom keywords on 2 of 13 = 0.1538 (paired McNemar p = 1.0); the declared kill does not fire and the declared 0.30 bar for building anything is not met, so the class closes. Mechanism, now measured: a failure report names the symptom and the environment, a fix states the cause and the change, and 0 of 13 rows share a 3-word run with their fix (E169) while the thread carries it at >= 0.8 on 12 of 13 -- the responder's prose is the bridge, and that semantic step is the strongest accessible alternative. No retriever proposed, so no prior-art screen run. F131 (control lesson plus five reproducible index defects), F132 (the closure), D115 (an index is declared as a surface with its query semantics).", "unlogged_changes": 0}, "host": "instance-20260717-0947", "kind": "session_end", "schema": "origin.session.event/1", "seq": 64, "session": "2026-10-16-005-e170-measure-ranked-reachability-of-a-pu", "ts": "2026-10-16T06:21:56+00:00"}
